Subject: [PATCH 06874/11362] [outer-loop] ARC g50t round-5: L3->L4, elevator
 mechanic reframed

Round-5 claude-fable-5 attempt on g50t solved L4, directly executing
round-4's "route the second clone through the socket AS A CLONE"
recommendation. Reframes the color-15 object entirely: it's a REMOTELY
CONTROLLED OCCUPANCY ELEVATOR, not a simple clone-selective reroute -- a
body waiting in the upper car at (26,38) is carried to the lower car at
(26,50) exactly when another body occupies the far-right endpoint at
(50,26). Winning choreography: clone A holds the color-8 door, clone B
reaches the remote endpoint, and the active runner enters the upper car
on clone B's final replay tick, rides down, and exits onto the goal.

Fresh-reset reproduce() gate confirmed reached_level=4. Independently
re-verified by the outer loop: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via a new
resolver priority branch, all 5 confirmed level=4, state=NOT_FINISHED.

L5 was mapped (two snapping shaft gates, a bottom-corridor gate, another
remote elevator) but not solved -- timing probes depleted the level timer
before the corrected choreography could run.

reproducible_total_levels 154 -> 155. arc_count_integrity_lint.py exit 0.

